        "actionableConclusion": [
          "Raw BRA/URY/ARG exclude the XQP interior and meet its boundary without overlap. Exact raw country selection would leave the entire raw island unassigned among these three.",
          "Existing approved current geometry also leaves the tested interior point and about 86.7 percent of the raw footprint unassigned; small edge coverages belong to all three adjacent mainland polygons, not a complete island ownership allocation.",
          "No verified previous whole-island attribution was found to copy. Adding XQP to BRA, URY or both would require an explicit display/ownership composition decision, not just higher-resolution replacement.",
          "Omitting XQP preserves non-assignment of the tested interior point, but does not preserve the exact old footprint and is not evidence of a deliberate approved exclusion. Do not silently interpret omission as permission to resolve or perpetuate the island gap.",
          "The American group also remains connected to French Guiana/FRA, so resolving XQP alone would not certify a closed raw replacement batch."
        ],
